{
  "name": "Geocode Spanish addresses in Google Sheets with Geo Govoy (batch, flag doubtful rows)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Geocode Spanish addresses in Google Sheets with Geo Govoy\n\nReads a sheet with an **address** column, geocodes it in batches of up to 1,000 with the Geo Govoy API (`POST /v2/geocode`, Spain only) and writes **lat, lon, status, confidence, normalized_address, next_action and reason** back to the same row. Rows that need review (no match, `next_action` not `accept`, or confidence < 0.8) are also copied to a **Review** tab.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a Google Sheet with a tab `Addresses` and these headers in row 1: `address | lat | lon | status | confidence | normalized_address | next_action | reason`. Add a tab `Review` with the same headers.\n2. In the 3 Google Sheets nodes, select your Google credential and paste the sheet URL.\n3. In **Geocode batch (Geo Govoy)**, create a **Header Auth** credential: Name `X-API-Key`, Value your Geo Govoy API key (free monthly allowance; request it at admin@govoy.es).\n4. Click **Execute workflow**.\n\n### Notes\n- Only rows with an empty `lat` are processed, so you can re-run it or swap the trigger for a Schedule Trigger.\n- Change `COLUMN` (Build batches) or `THRESHOLD` (One row per address) to adapt it.\n- 1 unit per distinct address; rejected requests are free. The HTTP node retries 3 times (5 s) on errors and 429.\n- `next_action` is `accept`, `confirm` (check with the customer) or `fix` (correct the address).\n- Docs: https://geo.govoy.es/docs",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "d86e9153-15df-4359-be19-ee60af982933",
      "name": "Read me",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -380,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "b49622a4-35b9-4bdf-b792-91999b01c384",
      "name": "When clicking 'Execute workflow'",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        140,
        100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "",
          "mode": "url"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "Addresses",
          "mode": "name"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "f406c510-3646-4f33-847d-36d642fa6531",
      "name": "Read addresses",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        360,
        100
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "googleSheetsOAuth2Api": {
          "name": "Google Sheets"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Sheet column with the address, and batch size (max 1,000 per request)\nconst COLUMN = 'address';\nconst BATCH = 1000;\n\n// Only rows with an address and an empty lat (so the workflow can be re-run safely)\nconst rows = $input.all()\n  .map((i) => i.json)\n  .filter((r) => String(r[COLUMN] ?? '').trim() !== '' && String(r.lat ?? '').trim() === '');\n\nconst batches = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < rows.length; i += BATCH) {\n  batches.push({\n    json: {\n      items: rows.slice(i, i + BATCH).map((r) => ({\n        external_id: String(r.row_number),\n        raw_address: String(r[COLUMN]).trim(),\n      })),\n    },\n  });\n}\nreturn batches;"
      },
      "id": "cbc406da-91d3-40b2-8a46-30fedd474436",
      "name": "Build batches of 1,000",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        580,
        100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://geo.govoy.es/v2/geocode",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ items: $json.items, top_k: 1 }) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 120000
        }
      },
      "id": "fa0a65a2-3761-4405-b29e-6908f0275c85",
      "name": "Geocode batch (Geo Govoy)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        800,
        100
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000,
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "name": "Geo Govoy API key"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Minimum confidence to accept an address without review\nconst THRESHOLD = 0.8;\n\nconst out = [];\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\n  for (const r of item.json.results ?? []) {\n    const c = (r.candidates ?? [])[0];\n    const confidence = c ? Number(c.confidence_score) : 0;\n    const needs_review = !c || r.next_action !== 'accept' || confidence < THRESHOLD;\n    out.push({\n      json: {\n        row_number: Number(r.external_id),\n        address: r.input?.raw_address ?? '',\n        lat: c ? c.lat : '',\n        lon: c ? c.lon : '',\n        status: r.status,\n        confidence: c ? Math.round(confidence * 1000) / 1000 : '',\n        normalized_address: c ? c.formatted_address : '',\n        next_action: r.next_action,\n        reason: (r.warnings ?? []).join(', '),\n        needs_review,\n      },\n    });\n  }\n}\nreturn out;"
      },
      "id": "793fe9f8-5dc2-4f70-8710-aabff2247310",
      "name": "One row per address",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
